WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:05.460
Okay, so I treat API documentation as pages with one job each,

2
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.460
from the quickstart to the error guide.

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:10.360
An OpenAPI file can generate the reference,

4
00:00:10.505 --> 00:00:15.465
but explaining what to do after a four-oh-nine is still my job.

5
00:00:15.465 --> 00:00:19.460
So my reference lists each response the endpoint returns,

6
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.565
with its cause and its fix.

7
00:00:21.565 --> 00:00:27.210
A four-oh-nine means the idempotency key was reused with a different body,

8
00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.242
so the fix is a new key.

9
00:00:29.242 --> 00:00:33.727
Then a script sends each documented case to the running service,

10
00:00:33.762 --> 00:00:37.787
so a changed status code fails the check before a developer hits it.
